---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Credits · mogkit"
  description="What we credit, what we built, and the provenance of every asset on the mogkit site."
>
  <article class="container-tight pt-16 sm:pt-20 pb-8">
    <Eyebrow>Credits</Eyebrow>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-halo tracking-tightest leading-[0.98] mt-4 lift-in lift-in-2">
      Provenance, plainly.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-chrome leading-relaxed lift-in lift-in-3">
      mogkit is built on the work of named people. This page tracks anything
      on the site that came from outside the project, plus the prototype
      decisions that shaped what shipped.
    </p>
  </article>

  <Section spacing="default">
    <div class="container-tight space-y-4">
      <Card padding="md">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-halo tracking-tight">Chrome surfboard hero</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
          The chrome board on the home page is generated procedurally — a
          tapered lathe with a Standard chrome material under a single key
          light. No third-party model is shipped with the site.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
          During design exploration we considered loading a Sketchfab-sourced
          GLB (a CC-BY-4.0 asset). We dropped it in favor of procedural
          geometry — smaller bundle, no licensing friction, and the
          single-light Voidchrome treatment lands the same intent. If a
          custom-modeled board ever ships here it'll be credited on this page.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card padding="md">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-halo tracking-tight">Methodology</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
          Every mogkit skill names the craft tradition it encodes in its
          frontmatter. The deepest debts:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Teresa Torres</strong> — Continuous Discovery Habits; the Opportunity Solution Tree.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Rob Fitzpatrick</strong> — The Mom Test.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Marty Cagan</strong> — INSPIRED, EMPOWERED.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Working Backwards (Bryar &amp; Carr)</strong> — six-pager and narrative-led planning.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Fisher &amp; Ury</strong> — Getting to Yes; the positions-vs-interests frame behind <code>stakeholder-map</code>.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Sean Ellis &amp; Morgan Brown</strong> — Hacking Growth; the North Star / input-metrics decomposition behind <code>metrics-tree</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </Card>

      <Card padding="md">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-halo tracking-tight">Typography &amp; iconography</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Inter Tight</strong> + <strong class="text-halo font-medium">Inter</strong> — Rasmus Andersson (Google Fonts, OFL).</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">JetBrains Mono</strong> — JetBrains (Google Fonts, OFL).</li>
          <li>The mogkit wordmark is plain typography; there's no logo lockup in v1.</li>
        </ul>
      </Card>

      <Card padding="md">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-halo tracking-tight">Software</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Astro</strong>, <strong class="text-halo font-medium">Tailwind</strong>, <strong class="text-halo font-medium">MDX</strong>, <strong class="text-halo font-medium">Pagefind</strong> — power the site.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">React Three Fiber</strong> + <strong class="text-halo font-medium">three.js</strong> — power the chrome surfboard hero.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Claude Code</strong> — the agent every mogkit skill runs inside.</li>
        </ul>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
